Unity DocSnap was previously published as source under the MIT Licence.
Everything up to and including the `v1.0.3` tag in the public repository's
history was released that way, that grant was irrevocable, and it still covers
every copy obtained under it. A copy of the MIT text is kept at the end of this
file so the history stays readable.

It does not extend to this distribution or to anything released after it. The
boundary is the tag, not the version number: this release is the first
published as a compiled assembly under this agreement.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1  Install and use. You may download, install and use Unity DocSnap in any
     number of your own Unity projects, personal or commercial, on the number
     of machines your edition allows (see section 2).

1.2  Own the output. Everything Unity DocSnap generates — the HTML site, the
     summaries, the JSON, the backups, the copied files — is yours. This
     licence claims nothing over it. Publish it, sell it, hand it to a client
     or to an AI assistant. No attribution is required for the output beyond
     the credit line the Free edition writes into the footer of the site it
     generates, which you may not remove while running the Free edition
     (see 3.3).

1.3  Redistribute inside your own team. You may copy the unmodified package to
     other machines inside your own organisation, provided each machine that
     uses a paid feature carries its own licence key.

1.4  Inspect it. You may read, decompile and analyse the package for the sole
     purpose of satisfying yourself that it is safe to run in your project, or
     of diagnosing a fault in it. You may not use what you learn to do
     anything section 3 forbids.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
2. THE EDITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1  Free. No key, no account, no payment, no network access. Free is licensed
     to you perpetually under this agreement for the features the Free edition
     enables.

2.2  Plus and Pro. Unlocked by a licence key purchased from
     https://amircollider.com. A key activates ONE machine at a time. Moving
     to another machine is self-service: release the old machine from
     "Unity DocSnap ▸ Licence & Pro Features", or from
     https://amircollider.com/license when that machine is gone.

2.3  Both paid editions are one-off purchases, not subscriptions, and include
     every 1.x update.

2.4  A licence key is personal to the purchaser. Sharing, publishing, reselling
     or sub-licensing a key is a breach of this agreement and the key will be
     revoked.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
--------------------------------------------------------------------

You may not:

3.1  Circumvent the licensing. Modify, patch, replace, hook, disable or in any
     other way bypass the code that decides which edition is active or which
     features it may use — whether by editing source, patching the compiled
     assembly, forging or altering a licence token, spoofing a machine
     identifier, redirecting the licence server, or any other means. Using a
     build in which this has been done, whoever did it, is equally a breach.

3.2  Use a paid feature without a valid licence for it. The list of which
     features belong to which edition is published in the README and shown in
     the Editor.

3.3  Remove the Free edition's credit line from a site generated by the Free
     edition. Any paid edition removes it automatically; that is one of the
     things a paid edition is.

3.4  Redistribute the package publicly. You may not upload Unity DocSnap, in
     whole or in part, modified or unmodified, to any public repository, asset
     store, package registry, file host, torrent or other distribution channel.
     Point people at the official repository instead.

3.5  Sell it or a derivative of it. You may not sell, rent, lease, sub-licence
     or offer Unity DocSnap as a service, nor create or distribute a product
     derived from it.

3.6  Strip the notices. You may not remove or alter any copyright notice,
     licence notice, authorship line or version marker in the package.

Nothing in section 3 is intended to restrict any right that applicable
mandatory law grants you and that a licence cannot lawfully take away. Where
your local law grants such a right, it prevails over the corresponding
sentence here and the rest of this agreement stays in force.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
4. REPORTING PROBLEMS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Bug reports, feature requests and security reports are welcome at
https://github.com/AmirCollider/UnityDocSnap/issues and, for security
specifically, through the process described in SECURITY.md. Reporting a
vulnerability in good faith through that process is not a breach of section
3.1, even where finding it required decompiling the package.


--------------------------------------------------------------------
5. TERMINATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1  This licence ends automatically if you breach section 3. On termination
     you must stop using Unity DocSnap and delete your copies. Anything you
     already generated with it stays yours (see 1.2).

5.2  A refunded or charged-back purchase ends the paid part of the licence.
     The tool then runs as Free; it does not stop working and it does not
     touch anything you generated.


